---
Add static analysis to CI pipeline.

Integrate cppcheck and/or clang-tidy with security-focused checks.
Fail build on critical findings.

## Tools
- cppcheck: --enable=warning,style,performance,portability --error-exitcode=1
- clang-tidy: cert-*, bugprone-*, security-*, misc-* checks
- Pick one or both for CI, run the other locally

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Static analysis runs in GitHub Actions CI
- [ ] Critical/error findings fail the build
- [ ] Warnings are reported but don't fail
- [ ] Suppressions file for known false positives (vendored deps)
- [ ] Local run script: ./scripts/lint.sh

## Test Plan
- [ ] Introduce a known bug (buffer overflow), verify CI catches it
- [ ] Verify vendored code (deps/) is excluded from analysis
- [ ] Verify all src/ files are analyzed
